<title>UK: Royal Doulton to cut UK workforce.</title>
<headline>Royal Doulton to cut UK workforce.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>British tableware maker Royal Doulton Plc said on Thursday it would cut its staff in Stoke-on-Trent, central England, by about 330 people out of a total workforce of 4,800 in the area.  </p>
<p>&quot;The strong pound has created a difficult worldwide trading climate for many manufacturers including ourselves, and it is essential that we aim to keep production, sales and stocks in balance,&quot; the company said in a brief statement.</p>
<p>Royal Doulton said it would reduce its staff with voluntary early retirement and redundancy programmes, as well as some lay-offs.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
